|}The '''1962 FIFA World Cup final''' was the deciding match of the [[1962 FIFA World Cup]]. The match was held at the [[Estadio Nacional Julio Martínez Prádanos|Estadio Nacional]] in [[Santiago]], and was contested by [[Czechoslovakia national football team|Czechoslovakia]] and [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]]. Brazil won the game 3–1 to record their second consecutive World Cup victory. Both teams had played each other during the group stage which ended in a goalless draw. This was the second World Cup final match featuring teams who had already competed against each other during the group stage (the first was the [[1954 FIFA World Cup final|1954 final]] between [[Hungary national football team|Hungary]] and [[Germany national football team|West Germany]]). This event was on Sunday, 17 June 1962.

This was the first final where the two countries had both previously appeared in the final.

This was only the second successful defence of the World Cup title in the history of the competition (after Italy in 1938) in spite of the absence of one of Brazil's star players of 1958, [[Pelé]], who was ruled out of action after being injured during the second match of the tournament.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2007/m=3/news=brazil-flying-high-with-little-bird-garrincha-502112.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150406194745/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2007/m=3/news=brazil-flying-high-with-little-bird-garrincha-502112.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=6 April 2015 |title=Brazil flying high with 'Little Bird' Garrincha |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=March 2007 |access-date=3 January 2018}}</ref>

The last surviving player on Czechoslovakia's side was [[Josef Jelínek]], who died on 29 November 2024, aged 83.<ref>{{cite news|last=Bartošová|first=Michaela|date=30 November 2024|title=Český fotbal truchlí: Zemřel Josef Jelínek, legenda Dukly a hrdina mistrovství světa v Chile|trans-title=Czech football mourns: Josef Jelínek, Dukla legend and hero of the World Cup in Chile, has died|url=https://cnn.iprima.cz/cesky-fotbal-truchli-zemrel-legendarni-utocnik-dukly-a-hrdina-z-mistrovstvi-sveta-454978|language=cs|website=[[CNN Prima News]]|access-date=30 November 2024|archive-date=4 December 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241204155649/https://cnn.iprima.cz/cesky-fotbal-truchli-zemrel-legendarni-utocnik-dukly-a-hrdina-z-mistrovstvi-sveta-454978|url-status=live}}</ref> As a consequence, Brazil's [[Amarildo (footballer, born 1939)|Amarildo]] is the last surviving player of the final.

==Match==

===Summary===
After 15 minutes, Brazil again found themselves a goal behind in the World Cup final, as a long ball from [[Tomáš Pospíchal]] was latched onto by [[Josef Masopust]] to put Czechoslovakia 1–0 ahead. However, just like the previous final four years earlier, Brazil soon hit back, equalising two minutes later through [[Amarildo (footballer, born 1939)|Amarildo]] after an error by the previously flawless Czechoslovak goalkeeper [[Viliam Schrojf]]. The Brazilians did not stop there and with goals from [[Zito (footballer, born 1932)|Zito]] and [[Vavá]] (another Schrojf error) midway through the second half, the Czechoslovaks could not get back into the game, with the match ending 3–1 to Brazil.<ref>[https://www.ceskatelevize.cz/porady/10337774070-finale-ms-ve-fotbalu-1962-ceskoslovensko-brazilie/21147129812/ Finále MS ve fotbalu 1962: Československo - Brazílie] {{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110210150628/https://www.ceskatelevize.cz/porady/10337774070-finale-ms-ve-fotbalu-1962-ceskoslovensko-brazilie/21147129812/ |date=10 February 2011 }}</ref>

